The founder, box 49153 (answer to 49107, which Misho told the code session
to put to Tornike): „you dont need approval to send thank you. just do it
automatically."

- sendHelperThanks replaces the yes/no card: the moment the owner says a
  helper's answer helped, the helper and every bridge of the chain get the
  approved 1692 line, once per ask (a card or day-14 row left behind is
  claimed; a thanked row never again). Nothing is asked of the owner; the
  row closes with no „ask again?" waiting.
- Three paths: the „helped" debrief, a goal closed as solved
  (thankForSolvedGoal), and — new — the owner's own line „<helper>-ის პასუხი
  დამეხმარა" naming exactly one answered, unthanked helper by the first word
  of the name they saved (thankHelperNamedIn; „არ დამეხმარა" never).
- A card offered before this ships still settles as before when tapped.
- §116 records the ruling. No new text.

